  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "Q1",
      "title": "Who moves ODH code into the Red Hat forks?",
      "text": "Keep open: identify the exact source branch, target branch, bot/configuration, schedule, conflict owner, approvals, and backport rules for each component. Do stable → downstream main → rhoai-3.6 actually apply to both?",
      "sources": [
        "eval-stable",
        "operator-stable",
        "rh-eval-build",
        "rh-workload-build"
      ],
      "owner": "Component maintainers / DevOps"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q2",
      "title": "Which TrustyAI tests actually block merges?",
      "text": "Controller, module smoke and Prow tests are configured. Prow e2e is path-triggered. The classic branch-protection endpoint was inaccessible and the branch-rules endpoint returned no rules for upstream TrustyAI; confirm Tide/branch protection, required contexts, approvals and override policy. ODH main rules show one approval; this does not establish stable/incubation requirements.",
      "sources": [
        "operator-ci",
        "module-ci",
        "prow",
        "operator-sync"
      ],
      "owner": "Repository / CI owners"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q3",
      "title": "Are module and workload images intentionally built from different branches?",
      "text": "EvalHub and TrustyAI workload builds target stable. The TrustyAI module build targets main, including the copy on stable. ODH installer manifests pin TrustyAI main. Confirm that this split is intentional and that a compatible module + workload + EvalHub set is tested together.",
      "sources": [
        "odh-eval-build",
        "odh-workload-build",
        "odh-module-build",
        "odh-module-stable",
        "manifest-pins"
      ],
      "owner": "TrustyAI / ODH maintainers"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q4",
      "title": "What makes an image set eligible for installer selection?",
      "text": "Digest pins and image-update PRs exist. Confirm which successful tests or policy verdicts gate a component digest nudge, who owns ODH Build Config updates, and what prevents mismatches between the selected image, module manifests, and provider ConfigMaps. The EvalHub ConfigMap sync workflow checks drift after main pushes and nightly; it does not itself promote changes.",
      "sources": [
        "manifest-pins",
        "odh-digests",
        "operator-nudge",
        "config-sync"
      ],
      "owner": "Build / integration owners"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q5",
      "title": "Which QE / Enterprise Contract verdicts are mandatory?",
      "text": "The source defines scan tasks and Early Gate testing, but that alone does not prove merge or stage enforcement. The inspected release integration-test YAML still names a 2.17 application. Confirm live 3.6 IntegrationTestScenarios, release policy, required BVT/e2e suites, exceptions and whether Early Gate is required.",
      "sources": [
